    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d519">

                <pb facs="0585" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg469"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1154.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sullivan to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 28, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Bobo, ex-Minister of the Interior of Haiti, has issued revolutionary call to the
                    Haitians from Monte Christi, where he makes headquarters. He makes attack on
                    proposed American control of customs in Haiti. He is secretly supported by
                    Arias, Dominican Minister of <pb facs="0586" n="470" xml:id="pg470"/> War.
                    Manifesto issued has tendency to create bad feeling against Americans both in
                    Dominican Republic and Haiti. I have informally called President Jiménes’
                    attention to Bobo’s conduct. President has commanded Bobo to leave Monte Christi
                    at once.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
